# Context And Session Management

## Context Health

- Use full file paths in implementation plans and final reports.
- Summarize key constraints before complex multi-step work.
- Refresh context when the task changes from analysis to implementation, or from implementation to review.
- If answer quality degrades or the same issue fails twice, stop and reassess context before continuing.

## Session Strategy

For large tasks, split work into independently verifiable sessions:

| Session | Goal | Persistence |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Understand structure and constraints | Rules, docs, or notes |
| 2 | Implement changes | Git diff and tests |
| 3 | Independent verification | Test results and review notes |

## Codebase Map

Large projects should maintain a lightweight `CODEBASE.md` at the project root:

```text
# Codebase Map
## Core Services
- services/api/       - REST API gateway
- services/payments/  - Payment processing
## Shared Libraries
- packages/types/     - Cross-service types
## Do Not Touch
- generated/          - Auto-generated files
```

The map should describe top-level structure only. Detailed constraints belong in nested rules or module docs.

## Noise Exclusion

Keep generated files, build artifacts, and third-party code out of routine search scope:

- `node_modules/`
- `dist/`
- `build/`
- `vendor/`
- `generated/`
- coverage outputs and temporary files

Commit exclusion rules when the whole team should share them.

## Configuration Iteration

Review agent configuration every three to six months or after major model releases. Separate rules that compensate for model limitations from rules that encode durable project conventions.
